        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Nine hospitals across five trusts in England have declared critical incidents in the past week, with all referencing flu, infectious diseases or winter pressures as contributing factors. Professor Sir Stephen Powis, the national medical director for NHS England, cited a \"quad-demic\" of illness as outbreaks of flu, Covid, norovirus and RSV add to pressure on hospitals.",
